    "created_at": "2015-09-05T15:14:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-05T15:14:00Z",
    "body": "This is fixing https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28123 right?\n\nA few editorial things:\n- wrap lines to 100 characters\n- double quote attributes\n- introduce new references and use them, instead of direct `<a href>`s\n- I think the `data-x` usage is incorrect. This isn't properly documented, and I might have it wrong, but my understanding is that you use `<dfn data-x=\"...\">` to define new terms, and `<span data-x=\"...\">` or just `<span>` to reference previously-defined terms. For terms defined in other specifications, see e.g. the lines like `The following features and terms are defined in the <cite>CSS Syntax</cite> specifications`.\n- Use https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/ instead of http://www.w3.org/TR/html-aria/. (Might also want to fix the mixed content on the latter, which in Firefox at least makes the page appear really bad.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
