    "created_at": "2015-09-06T14:59:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-06T14:59:27Z",
    "body": "> So will there never be a Recommendation published there? What does that mean?\n\nSo my understanding is that given a TR address https://www.w3.org/TR/html-aria/ even if a Rec is ever published, if/when Steve makes any updates after that, he could still immediately push the update to  https://www.w3.org/TR/html-aria/ and it would immediately replace the Rec version at that address.\n\nIn other words, the (undated) TR version is not frozen.\n\nThe only things that are frozen are the dated URLs; so that if the Rec of this spec were published on 2015/09/02, then the dated https://www.w3.org/TR/2015/WD-html-aria-20150902/ URL is always there as the URL representing that state of the Rec—and anybody who wants to use/cite the Rec version (snapshot) rather than the Living Document could (should) use that https://www.w3.org/TR/2015/WD-html-aria-20150902/ URL.\n\nBut everybody else can just continue using/citing the Living Document at https://www.w3.org/TR/html-aria/ with the confidence that Steve will continue to be able to maintain it such that if/when he makes further changes, he can freely push them there any time to update it.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
